=== full commit message ===
style: bring the monorepo green under ultracite 7.10.1

`bun run check` reported 491 errors after the ultracite bump. 323 were
mechanical (useSortedKeys, useSortedAttributes, useSortedClasses) and came
out with `ultracite fix`. The rest are fixed here:

- noJsxPropsBind (69): useCallback, or a extracted row/tab component where
  the handler closed over a .map item.
- noLeakedRender (33): `cond && <x/>` -> `cond ? <x/> : null`.
- noUnnecessaryConditions (17): BlogFrontmatter's defaulted fields are
  optional now, so the `?? []` fallbacks are honest; the collaboration
  avatar uses `||` because the auth shim yields "" rather than null; the
  interval refs compare `!== null`, since biome reads
  `useRef(null).current` as always-null from the initializer.
- noArrayIndexKey (11): identity assigned outside the JSX instead of keying
  on the render index.
- noExportedImports (10): dropped the re-export hops in the masterclass
  demos and pointed importers at the source modules — re-exporting only
  trades this rule for noBarrelFile.
- noAwaitInLoops (8): parallelised the five independent loops in
  scripts/initialize.ts. Three stay serial with a stated reason: one git
  subprocess per file, >1000 concurrent copyFile descriptors, and a demo
  that deliberately models a serial pipeline.
- noRedundantDefaultExport (4): email templates are default-only, which is
  what React Email's preview needs; importers updated.
- useDestructuring (8), noNonNullAssertion (3), and one each of
  noNestedTernary, useTopLevelRegex, useImageSize, noNestedPromises,
  noUselessCatchBinding.

Behaviour is unchanged except in two places, both improvements: the
notifications popover mounts off state instead of reading a ref during
render, and RhythmFigure now takes the intrinsic size its <img> needs.

check, typecheck, test and build are all green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Entire-Checkpoint: 3ef8a8b8ce31

